rem Right-angled Triangles that Share a
rem Cathetus
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=176
rem Find the least cathetus shared by
rem exactly Ways right-angled triangles

use numbers
use linalg
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Ways integer = 47547

rem A cathetus n gives (d(n^2) - 1) / 2
rem triangles, or (d(n^2 / 4) - 1) / 2
rem if n is even, d counting divisors.
rem So the odd divisor count 2 Ways + 1
rem is a product of factors 2 e + 1, one
rem per prime. Try every grouping of its
rem prime factors, give the largest
rem group to the smallest prime.
F = (2 * Ways + 1) factors array
K = F len
Count = (array shape K fill K) reduce *
Ids' = 0 till Count array
Bases = array shape K fill (K 2 max)
Lab' = (Ids Bases digits) transpose
Pos = 0 till K array
Row' = Lab reshape Count 1 K
Hit' = Row equal (Pos reshape 1 K 1)
Fs' = F reshape 1 1 K
Gp = (Hit choose Fs 1) reduce * rank 1
Gp = Gp sort .descending
Pr = primes take (K + 1) array
Two' = (Pos equal 0) choose 1 0
Even' = ((Gp - 1) // 2 + Two)
Even' = (Pr take K) ** Even
Odd' = (Pr drop 1) ** ((Gp - 1) // 2)
Ne' = Even reduce * rank 1
No' = Odd reduce * rank 1
Answer = (concat Ne No) min
Answer print
